SamIAm wrote:

> I recall reading in various FAQ's that the player was going to
> "#ability" or something - I started to get the impression that there
> was some active thing I needed to do to "activate" my increased
> skills.
> 
> I know I'm not explaining this clearly, I'm sorry.  For example, my
> weapons skills, my two-handed staff is always on "basic" even after I
> get to level 12 or something.  Is that because I haven't "turned on"
> my skill in that ability?
> 
> I would think this would be an automatic skill increase, but I would
> hate to keep playing and lose the benefit because of ignorance.  Can
> anyone help me understand this?  Thanks.


The simple answer is: Yes.

The command to do this is #enhance. You can then improve those skills 
that you've used enough. But only if you have free skill slots.

You only get 1 skill slot per level change. So 5th level character has 4 
skill slots and 30th (the max) has 29 skill slots to use.

